<title>INDIA: India M&amp;M 96/97 1st half net up 25 pct.</title>
<headline>India M&amp;M 96/97 1st half net up 25 pct.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Six months to September 1996</p>
<p>		(in million rupees unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit	     924.30    vs	 738.10</p>
<p>    Total income	14,670.00    vs    11,930.00</p>
<p>    Net sales	   14,286.19    vs    11,547.05</p>
<p>    Shr (in rupees)	 18.16    vs	  15.73</p>
<p>    Other income	 3,82.75     vs	 387.99</p>
<p>    Expenditure	 12,732.18    vs    10,310.32</p>
<p>    Interest costs	 303.12    vs	 201.33</p>
<p>    Gross profit	 1,633.64    vs     1,423.39</p>
<p>    Depreciation	   254.30    vs	 193.31</p>
<p>    Taxation		 455.00    vs	 492.00</p>
<p>Note: Utility vehilces and tractor maker Mahindra &amp; Mahindra said earnings per share was adjusted after a bonus issue of two shares for three in February 1996.</p>
<p>-- Bombay newsroom + 91-22-265 9000</p>
</text>
